# What the live session is: a host that boots, displays the installer and
# installs. It is not a copy of the desktop the installer writes — the desktop
# set lives in the installer's own lists (installer/backend/install/{installbase,
# installdesktop}) and the ISO build reads them too
# (docker/scripts/build-iso.sh → `go run ./backend/scripts/pkg-list.go`), so the
# offline mirror holds the union of this file and those lists.
#
# Two consequences for anyone editing this:
#   - A package only the *installed* system needs belongs in the installer's
#     lists, not here. It reaches the mirror from there, and an install gets it
#     without network. (That is where base-devel, firefox, dux-shell, mpv and
#     the distro's own apps live.)
#   - A package the installer *runs* has to stay here, because it runs in this
#     session: formatting, encrypting, snapshotting, registering the firmware
#     entry, and copying rEFInd's assets out of /usr/share/refind.
#
# What is left is what that takes.

# Base system — the live session's own kernel, initramfs and boot entries.
# syslinux/grub are the profile's bootmodes; edk2-shell and memtest86+-efi are
# the UEFI shell and memory-test entries the boot menu offers.
base
linux-lts
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
arch-install-scripts
mkinitcpio-archiso
qemu-guest-agent
spice-vdagent
edk2-shell
memtest86+-efi
syslinux
grub

# The tools the installer runs here, against the disk it is writing.
util-linux
gptfdisk
parted
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
btrfs-progs
lvm2
cryptsetup
snapper
pv

# Bootloader. The installer copies rEFInd's EFI binary and icons out of this
# session's /usr/share/refind, so the package has to be installed here, not
# only in the mirror; efibootmgr registers it in the firmware's boot order.
refind
efibootmgr

# The splash whose bar tracks real mount milestones (the aelum-live hook), and
# the live user's passwordless sudo.
plymouth
sudo

# The session the installer draws in. webkit2gtk-4.1 is the installer GUI's
# runtime (it pulls gtk3); hyprpaper shows the brand wallpaper behind it.
hyprland
greetd
greetd-agreety
webkit2gtk-4.1
hyprpaper
adwaita-cursors

# A terminal beside the installer: the live Hyprland config binds Super+Return
# to kitty and keeps its palette in step with the installer's light/dark
# toggle (aelum-theme-watch.sh), and its config asks for JetBrains Mono.
kitty
ttf-jetbrains-mono
nano

# Small things the live session itself uses: the display's brightness
# (brightnessctl / ddcutil — there is nothing else to reach them with during an
# install), compressed RAM for the pacstrap phase, and jq for the live scripts.
brightnessctl
ddcutil
zram-generator
jq

# Network — not needed to install (every package comes from the embedded
# mirror), but an install usually wants to be able to update afterwards, and a
# live session with no network cannot even fetch a PKGBUILD.
networkmanager
iwd
wireless-regdb

# The live session's SSH. This profile enables sshd.service and drops in
# /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10-archiso.conf for it (root, empty password), and the
# whole QEMU harness drives the guest through it (host 2222 → guest 22):
# test-install.sh waits for sshd before it starts, and verify-installed.sh runs
# inside the guest over SSH. openssh used to arrive as a dependency of gcr-4,
# which is precisely the accident an explicit list exists to prevent: the
# enabled unit and the config file stayed, the package did not.
openssh

# The fonts the installer's own UI renders: all 28 of its languages. Its icons
# are a woff2 subset embedded in its CSS, so no system icon font is needed.
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-cjk
